Exploratory multiplicity check on the directional E1 contrasts: Holm-Bonferroni and Benjamini-Hochberg over the v1 §4 predicted-non-zero contrasts, one family per stage, one-sided p-values from the main analysis' world bootstrap

analysis.multiplicity recomputes each contrast's per-world item differences through the same code path as e1.contrasts (rendered.contrast_vectors), takes the bootstrap draws behind the stored interval (scoring.stats.world_bootstrap_draws, the body of world_bootstrap unchanged), refuses to go on unless the recomputed estimate and interval equal e1_metrics.json, and reads a one-sided p-value off the draws. Exploratory: not part of prereg v1 or v2, no verdict changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
